From 4316d0fc6f6794e065e3c95726dae5db1ab1999f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:49:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Scheduler] Prefill yield: a long prompt's aligned chunk
 gives its step to short prompts and held first tokens

With aligned prefill chunks a long prompt's whole chunk takes the step's
budget beside the decode rows, so a request that arrives while it
prefills waits for its last chunk (about 19 s behind a 131K prompt on
the ring, 200 s behind 1M). --prefill-yield short lets a step carry
instead the waiting prompts whose prefill finishes within one chunk and,
with sink rejection, the first decode step of a prompt that just
prefilled. The long prompt's chunks keep their boundaries; only the step
a chunk runs in changes. A long prompt stops yielding after
--prefill-yield-limit-s (10 s) until its next chunk runs. Off by default;
with nothing short waiting a step schedules exactly as before.
